 "intro_html": "The onigiri you grill: the rice is seasoned with soy sauce, sugar and sesame oil before shaping, the triangles are pressed firmer than usual, then pan-grilled on parchment until every side is a <b>crisp, deep golden-brown crust</b> — and brushed with soy at the end so it lacquers in the pan. Crunchy outside, soft and steaming inside. For the shaping itself (by hand or with a mold), see <a href=\"onigiri.html\">onigiri</a>.",
