 "steps": [
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Soak the rice 20–30 minutes, then cook it with the water in a rice cooker or a heavy pot — see <a href=\"onigiri.html\">onigiri</a> for the pot method.</li><li>This makes about <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"990\" data-s=\"0\">990 g</span> of cooked rice: nine <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"110\" data-s=\"0\">110 g</span> onigiri.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-1",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Cook the rice",
    "diagram": null,
    "diagram_title": "Diagram",
    "how": [],
    "illustration": "illustrations/yaki-onigiri/1.webp?v=080049e1a1",
    "photo": null,
    "result": null,
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 1,
   "part": "Rice",
   "part_id": "part-rice",
   "time": "~1 h with soaking",
   "time_html": "<span>~1 h with soaking</span>",
   "title": "Cook the rice",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"cup\" data-a=\"2.25\">2¼ cups</span>",
     "name_html": "Japanese short-grain rice"
    },
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"cup\" data-a=\"2.5\">2½ cups</span><span class=\"qalt\"> (<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"ml\" data-a=\"600\" data-alt=\"1\">600 ml</span>)</span>",
     "name_html": "Water (rice)"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Stir the soy sauce and sugar together and microwave 30–60 seconds until hot; whisk until the sugar dissolves. Stir in the sesame oil and salt.</li><li>Hot rice into a large bowl, pour the seasoning over and fold it through with the rice paddle in a <b>slicing motion</b> — don’t mash.</li><li>Making some <b>miso</b> ones? Set aside <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"110\" data-s=\"0\">110 g</span> of plain rice for each before you season — the miso glaze goes on plain rice.</li><li>Let it cool just until you can hold it; it must still be warm to shape.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-2",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Season the rice",
    "diagram": null,
    "diagram_title": "Diagram",
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Soy and sugar, microwaved hot and whisked; then the sesame oil and salt.",
      "src": "illustrations/yaki-onigiri/2-how1.webp?v=0beef8a686"
     },
     {
      "caption": "Fold it through the hot rice with a slicing motion — don't mash.",
      "src": "illustrations/yaki-onigiri/2-how2.webp?v=c132e1783b"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/yaki-onigiri/2.webp?v=694a88f4e9",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 2,
   "part": "Rice",
   "part_id": "part-rice",
   "time": "~5 min",
   "time_html": "<span>~5 min</span>",
   "title": "Season the rice",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tbsp\" data-a=\"3\">3 tbsp</span>",
     "name_html": "Soy sauce (rice)"
    },
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tbsp\" data-a=\"1\">1 tbsp</span>",
     "name_html": "Sugar"
    },
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tbsp\" data-a=\"1\">1 tbsp</span>",
     "name_html": "Toasted sesame oil (rice)"
    },
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tsp\" data-a=\"0.25\">¼ tsp</span>",
     "name_html": "Kosher salt"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Shape nine triangles of about <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"110\" data-s=\"0\">110 g</span>, by hand or in a wet mold (fill to the top edge, lid on, push down until you feel resistance, flip out onto parchment) — see <a href=\"onigiri.html\">onigiri</a>.</li><li>Then press each one again with wet hands, <b>firmer than a normal onigiri</b>: left hand underneath squeezing the sides, right hand a “mountain” on top; press, roll the corner toward you, repeat for all three corners, then 2–3 more times. Loose ones fall apart in the pan.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-3",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Shape firm triangles",
    "diagram": null,
    "diagram_title": "Diagram",
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Shape 110 g triangles by hand or in a wet mold.",
      "src": "illustrations/yaki-onigiri/3-how1.webp?v=d7647b24c1"
     },
     {
      "caption": "Then press each one again, firmer than usual: right hand a roof on top, left hand squeezing the sides.",
      "src": "illustrations/yaki-onigiri/3-how2.webp?v=68f55a6a33"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/yaki-onigiri/3.webp?v=65e98c1c6e",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 3,
   "part": "Shape",
   "part_id": "part-shape",
   "time": "~8 min",
   "time_html": "<span>~8 min</span>",
   "title": "Shape firm triangles",
   "uses_rows": []
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Line a large frying pan with parchment and set the onigiri on it, a little apart. Medium-low heat.</li><li>Leave each side alone until it’s <b>crisp and browned</b> before you turn it — two silicone spatulas, one side at a time. Moving them early breaks them.</li><li>Turn them onto every side, including the edges, until the whole outside is a crisp golden-brown crust.</li></ul>",
   "heat": {
    "label": "medium-low",
    "label_html": "<span>medium-low</span>",
    "off": false
   },
   "id": "step-4",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Grill until crisp",
    "diagram": null,
    "diagram_title": "Diagram",
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Leave each side until it's crisp and browned, then turn it with two spatulas.",
      "src": "illustrations/yaki-onigiri/4-how1.webp?v=c1e9ffe6f2"
     },
     {
      "caption": "Stand them on their edges too, until the whole outside is crisp.",
      "src": "illustrations/yaki-onigiri/4-how2.webp?v=84b3383c92"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/yaki-onigiri/4.webp?v=a8eb3d4feb",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 4,
   "part": "Grill",
   "part_id": "part-grill",
   "time": "~12 min",
   "time_html": "<span>~12 min</span>",
   "title": "Grill until crisp",
   "uses_rows": []
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Stir the soy sauce and sesame oil together. Turn the heat to low (or off).</li><li>Brush one side, turn it glaze-side down onto the parchment, brush the top. A minute or so per side until it lacquers and darkens — it burns fast once the glaze is on.</li></ul>",
   "heat": {
    "label": "low",
    "label_html": "<span>low</span>",
    "off": false
   },
   "id": "step-5",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Soy glaze",
    "diagram": null,
    "diagram_title": "Diagram",
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Heat low: brush the top with the soy glaze.",
      "src": "illustrations/yaki-onigiri/5-how1.webp?v=0e73efbddb"
     },
     {
      "caption": "Turn it glaze-side down onto the parchment, then brush the other side.",
      "src": "illustrations/yaki-onigiri/5-how2.webp?v=dd0a66f311"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/yaki-onigiri/5.webp?v=906deb0741",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 5,
   "part": "Grill",
   "part_id": "part-grill",
   "time": "~3 min",
   "time_html": "<span>~3 min</span>",
   "title": "Soy glaze",
